The [#4471 page](/kb/incidents/4471) says one issue and one fix queued. That is wrong. The reports
merged into #4471 hold two problems with two different causes. The parser fix ("parse dd/mm for eu locales") could not
fix the other one.

<Callout>
Engineering closed #4471 on 5 October. Parser: **fixed** (fix(dates): parse dd/mm for eu locales). Hint: **won't fix**, because the booking-v3 form is retired. Issues 1 and 2 in this repo are closed with those outcomes.
</Callout>

## The two problems

1. **Parser reads dates month first** ([issue 1](https://github.com/ReaziS/megadev-training/issues/1)). A day-first tenant gets day and month flipped. This is the cause #4471 is named for. Fixed by engineering. It is the largest group in the table below (`parser`).
2. **The booking-v3 form hints MM/DD/YYYY** ([issue 2](https://github.com/ReaziS/megadev-training/issues/2)). Tenants that write the day first type what the hint tells them, month first, and the form reads it their way. The parser is not involved, so the parser fix does not help. This is the `hint` row.

## What was merged

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

Of the `parser` row, these reports the desk read as a one-day move. They are counted under `parser`, as the desk counts them. Their wording points at time zones, so check that when the parser is fixed:

<OneDayMove ticket={4471} />

## How to tell them apart

Do not use the intake tag. It is a guess from the reporter's browser and is wrong for dozens of reports. Look up the tenant: its locale tells you whether it writes the day first, and its booking form tells you which hint its people saw. Then check the channel: `form` at a booking-v3 tenant is `hint`. 

## Lessons

- A big ticket is not always one bug reported many times. Merging on the subject line hid two problems under one.
- Count once per problem, not once per ticket.

